  "bodyTypst": "The function $f$ is differentiable for all real numbers. The point $lr((3 \\, frac(1,4)))$ is on the graph of $y = f(x)$, and the slope at each point $(x \\, y)$ on the graph is given by $frac(d y,d x)= y^(2)(6 - 2 x)$.\n\n(a) Find $frac(d^(2) y,d x^(2))$ and evaluate it at the point $lr((3 \\, frac(1,4)))$.\n\n(b) Find $y = f(x)$ by solving the differential equation $frac(d y,d x)= y^(2)(6 - 2 x)$ with the initial condition $f(3)= frac(1,4)$.",
